{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.SkeinHorizonLowerBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinHorizonLowerBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationBridge"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_polyObservable_or_not_horizon_cost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_polyObservable_or_not_horizon_cost","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinHorizonLowerBound.lean#L132-L144","doc":"**Dichotomy (query-hard XOR shortcuttable).** Fixing an input whose horizon\nexceeds the budget, a system cannot both admit the exponential lower bound\n`hcost` and a polynomial shortcut. The lower bound lives exactly where no\nalgebraic shortcut does — the decision-tree side, witnessed by `treeSearch`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.no_horizon_cost_of_polyObservable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.no_horizon_cost_of_polyObservable","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinHorizonLowerBound.lean#L118-L130","doc":"**A polynomial shortcut refutes the horizon lower bound.** If the observation\nis reachable within a budget `poly` the horizon exceeds\n(`PolyObservable poly P` with `poly (len P) < 3^{len P}`), then the\nexponential lower bound `hcost` cannot hold for `P`. Contrapositive of\n`not_polyObservable_of_horizon_cost`: an efficiently-shortcuttable (algebraic)\nobservation is incompatible with a `3^{len}` lower bound — the structural core\nof why an algebraic invariant cannot separate the classes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.treeSearch_haltsObserved_not_polyObservable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.treeSearch_haltsObserved_not_polyObservable","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinHorizonLowerBound.lean#L73-L76","doc":"The separation, packaged: observed-halting **and** not poly-observable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.treeSearch_not_polyObservable_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.treeSearch_not_polyObservable_id","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinHorizonLowerBound.lean#L63-L71","doc":"**The horizon separation is inhabited.** `treeSearch d` at leaf `0` is\nobserved-halting yet **not** poly-observable under the identity (linear)\nbudget: a concrete, unconditional exponential separation between\n`HaltsObserved` and `PolyObservable`, with `hcost` proved rather than assumed.\nAn honest query / decision-tree lower bound — **not** a proof of P ≠ NP (the\ngeneral lower bound remains barred by algebrization). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.treeSearch_haltsObserved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.treeSearch_haltsObserved","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinHorizonLowerBound.lean#L57-L61","doc":"`treeSearch d` **is** observed-halting — the observation is reached, at step\n`3^d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.treeSearch_hcost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.treeSearch_hcost","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinHorizonLowerBound.lean#L44-L55","doc":"**The exponential lower bound `hcost`, discharged.** Starting from leaf `0`,\nthe observation matches the normal form only at step `3^d = 3^{len}` — the\nobserver must visit every leaf. Provable because the model is decision-tree\n(query) complexity, not general circuit complexity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.treeSearch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.treeSearch","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinHorizonLowerBound.lean#L33-L42","doc":"**Ternary-resolution search at depth `d`.** The state is a step counter, each\nstep advances one leaf of the depth-`d` resolution tree (`n ↦ n + 1`), the\nfiltration is the depth `d`, and the observation matches the normal form\n`3^d` only at the last of the `3^d` leaves. The decision-tree model in which\nthe exponential horizon lower bound is genuinely provable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.succ_iterate_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.succ_iterate_zero","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinHorizonLowerBound.lean#L27-L31","doc":"Iterating `n ↦ n + 1` from `0` reaches `k` after `k` steps. ","signatureChunk":0}]}